			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1475097">
									

<p>This is kind of an odd stance to me. The Foundation routinely carries out human experimentation, and not just on easy-to-hate criminals. The whole point of the Foundation is moral ambiguity; what lengths are you willing to go to in order to keep horror and chaos at bay? You could argue that they actually <em>did</em> make the ethical decision here, since the human-rat thing will eliminate the need to use multiple test subjects in the future; one (albeit horrible) life versus many lives.</p>
<p>I'm certainly not trying to talk anyone into liking this if they don't like it, but the Foundation isn't a nice organization at all. Even allowing for personal headcanon, I think there would be more of this sort of thing than &quot;nice&quot; things.</p>

